9. TASK 5 — STORE-SPECIFIC WEBSITE ORDER ROUTING
============================================================

When an online order belongs to Store A:

Store A must receive/manage it.

When an online order belongs to Store B:

Store B must receive/manage it.

The order must carry the correct Store ID throughout its lifecycle.

Order:

WEBSITE
→ STORE IDENTIFICATION
→ ORDER CREATION
→ STORE-SPECIFIC QUEUE
→ STORE-SPECIFIC PROCESSING
→ PURCHASE/DISPENSE
→ BILLING
→ DELIVERY
→ COMPLETION

A central management device may view/manage multiple stores.

But every operation must execute against the correct Store ID.

If a central user selects Store A and changes an order:

the change must be recorded against Store A.

If Store B is selected:

the operation must not touch Store A.

